From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:35:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: allocate DSA metadata before open

Backport the DSA metadata allocation ordering from the Linux
preparation. Metadata allocation can fail. Do it before PHY connection,
DMA startup, NAPI and queue activation so an allocation error leaves the
conduit closed. The later block still disables hardware tagging for a
non-DSA or XDP path.

Keep the original NETSYS generation condition: newer NETSYS devices
return before using these metadata destinations and must remain
independent of allocation failures for unused destinations.

Assisted-by: Codex (OpenAI GPT-6)
Signed-off-by: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -4140,6 +4140,13 @@ static int mtk_open(struct net_device *d
 
 	ppe_num = eth->soc->ppe_num;
 
+	if (!mtk_is_netsys_v2_or_greater(eth) &&
+	    (mtk_uses_dsa(dev) || mtk_uses_ralink_dsa(dev)) && !eth->prog) {
+		err = mtk_dsa_metadata_init(eth);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+	}
+
 	err = phylink_of_phy_connect(mac->phylink, mac->of_node, 0);
 	if (err) {
 		netdev_err(dev, "%s: could not attach PHY: %d\n", __func__,
@@ -4202,11 +4209,7 @@ static int mtk_open(struct net_device *d
 	if (mtk_is_netsys_v2_or_greater(eth))
 		return 0;
 
-	if ((mtk_uses_dsa(dev) || mtk_uses_ralink_dsa(dev)) && !eth->prog) {
-		err = mtk_dsa_metadata_init(eth);
-		if (err)
-			return err;
-	} else {
+	if ((!mtk_uses_dsa(dev) && !mtk_uses_ralink_dsa(dev)) || eth->prog) {
 		/* Hardware DSA untagging and VLAN RX offloading need to be
 		 * disabled if at least one MAC does not use DSA.
 		 */
